# Corpus unit bbox/C06 — gap (negative-result; noninferiority_comparison -> null_comparison dual)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/bbox.yaml C06 (negative-result; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: selecting
# positive samples via a GPT-4 judge (no ground-truth labels) is competitive with ground-truth
# selection — max accuracy gap 1.77 points over 4 datasets, well under the 5-point falsification
# margin.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * A negative-result "competitive with / no meaningful difference" claim is genuinely the
#     negation of a comparison conclusion, so it lowers through the null_comparison dual:
#     conclusion not_better(ai_feedback, ground_truth_labels, reasoning_accuracy, bbox_datasets).
#     Only this one arg-conclusion side appears; the positive better() side is NOT declared, so no
#     contrary pair is instantiated and no mutual rebut edges are forced (attack completeness holds
#     vacuously).
#   * The annotation's mandatory CQ3 is unmet-gap: no variance/repeats justify the 1.77-point
#     equivalence margin. A non-inferiority claim needs power to detect a difference, so this maps
#     onto null_comparison's mandatory adequate_power(e01) -> unmet. An open mandatory obligation is
#     an IncompleteArgument rejection -> E2-style gap.
#   * CQ1 (arms identical except positive-sample selection) discharges baseline_parity; CQ2 (no
#     ground-truth leakage through the judge) discharges measurement_validity. Both leaves are on
#     the page. The optional best-of-two-sizes CQ4 is omitted.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact bbox at sha256:bb06e592cef6
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c06
  nl      = "Selecting positive samples via a GPT-4 judge (no ground-truth labels) is competitive with ground-truth selection: max accuracy gap 1.77 points over 4 datasets, well under the 5-point falsification margin; no variance reported"
  formal  = not_better(ai_feedback, ground_truth_labels, reasoning_accuracy, bbox_datasets)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(e01, compares(ai_feedback, ground_truth_labels, reasoning_accuracy, bbox_datasets, null))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C06, Table-2, logic/experiments.md#E01-Metrics]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(ai_feedback, ground_truth_labels, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-4]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(reasoning_accuracy, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-4]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: adequate_power(e01) has no honest leaf — E01 reports single best-of-two
# numbers with no repeats or confidence intervals (CQ3, unmet-gap), so the 1.77-point equivalence
# margin is uncalibrated against noise — and corpus-v1 makes power mandatory for null_comparison.
# The claim's complete-support set is therefore empty.)

status c06

# ==============================================================================================
